WEBVTT

NOTE On-screen visual text only; this approved video has no audio track.

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:07.700
In this trace, speech stops at zero and the turn commits after 300 milliseconds.

2
00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:14.700
Playout starts at 780: another 480 milliseconds elapse after the commit.

3
00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:23.000
On the same clock, total waiting is 300 plus 480. It is not the model’s TTFT.

4
00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:30.700
STT already runs while the user speaks. Its full duration is not added again afterwards.

5
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:37.700
The first text starts TTS while the model continues generating the rest.

6
00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:47.000
Here first playout arrives at 700 milliseconds. The full processing bars overlap.

7
00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:54.700
The client reads 1000 and the server 1090. Subtraction gives 90, but mixes clocks.

8
00:00:54.700 --> 00:01:01.700
In this example, a known offset of 80 leaves a represented interval of 10.

9
00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:10.000
Without reconciling clocks, that subtraction does not measure latency. Matching IDs is not enough.

10
00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:17.700
A1 is generated at 600 milliseconds. It still needs transport and a playback queue.

11
00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:24.700
It arrives at 650, but playout starts at 700 in this trace.

12
00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:33.000
Name the observed boundary. A server acknowledgement does not prove physical hearing.

13
00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:40.700
These twenty synthetic turns include eighteen at 400 milliseconds and two at 1600.

14
00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:47.700
The mean is 520. Nearest-rank P95 is 1600.

15
00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:56.000
Segment by channel and conditions. Slow turns can have a different failure mechanism.

16
00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:03.700
The illustrative budget totals 700 milliseconds: 300 for the turn and 400 for the rest.

17
00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:10.700
Reducing model time from 180 to 90 brings the total to 610, not half.

18
00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:19.000
Check quality and premature endings too. Less waiting cannot compensate for a misunderstood request.

